        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0389" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg377"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.00/1157: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-04-28T14:00:00-00:44">April 28, 1942—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:59 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>136. Secretary of State Simpson states that President Barclay is anxious to
                    adjourn Liberian Legislature which has been in continuous session since last
                    October, longest in history, in view of his understanding that defense forces
                    would be in Liberia by end of April, he would like to know when conditions will
                    permit him to submit agreement to Legislature for approval.</p>
                <p>Legislature, to my knowledge, is being held for express purpose of submission of
                    agreement which to avoid publicity, it was agreed to withhold until adequate
                    defense forces reached Liberia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
